{%- comment -%}
===============================================================================
cancellation_notes.liquid — emit a cancelled appointment's FULL note set as JSON
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS EXISTS
The ServiceMinder Open API cannot see appointment-level notes. Verified
2026-08-29 against KTU appointment 51051472 (Garret Starr, cancelled 8/21):

  appointments/find      -> "Notes": null, "UpdateNote": null
  appointments/query     -> no note field at all; CancelReasonId: null
  contacts/locate        -> ONE note (the "Booking Details" intake blurb)
  download kind=appointments -> no Notes column

Meanwhile the SM UI shows an Appointment Note written by Ben Yabra on 8/20:
"Client wrote 'I tried to write in and tell them I wanted it last week. Not
this week' and then I both called client with no answer and also texted him
advising that we can reschedule if he'd still like. No reply back"

That note IS the cancellation reason. Every API path we have is blind to it, so
the intranet's Appointment Recovery tab was showing the pre-sale intake blurb
under a "cancel reason" header instead — i.e. reading as though he cancelled
because he wants new cabinets.

Liquid CAN see it. Per ServiceMinder's Liquid Objects reference, Appointment
exposes:
    appointment_notes  List<AppointmentNote>
    notes              List<Note>   {id,title,body,private,created_at,created_by}
    notes_summary      String
    customer_notes     String
    cancel_reason      IdName       <- the LABEL, not just the id
    contact.notes      List<Note>

cancel_reason.name is worth the whole exercise on its own: there is NO
cancel-reason lookup endpoint on this API (probed cancelreasons,
settings/cancelreasons, lookups/cancelreasons, appointmentcancelreasons — all
return HTTP 200 with an empty body). Liquid is the only place the id->label map
is visible, so "reason id 3523" finally becomes a human sentence.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO INSTALL (ServiceMinder UI — cannot be done through the API)

  Control Panel -> Notifications -> Appointment Cancelled
    * Add a delivery to the intranet ingest address.
    * Paste this template as the BODY. Set the format to plain text, not HTML —
      an HTML body will entity-escape the JSON and break the parser.
    * Subject line, exactly:  SM-CANCEL {{ appointment.id }}

  Do this once per brand (KTU and BTU) — notifications are per-organization.

The ingest-email webhook already lands mail in `inbox_emails`; Goldeneye
step 5b(a) picks the row up from there by the SM-CANCEL subject prefix.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT CONTRACT
One JSON object between the two sentinel lines. The sentinels matter: mail
gateways append footers and disclaimers, so the parser slices between them
rather than trusting the whole body to be JSON.

Private notes are INCLUDED and flagged `"private": true` — a rep's candid
"customer was furious about the quote" is exactly the signal Appointment
Recovery needs. The intranet must not surface a private note to a customer-
facing view; that filtering is the consumer's job, not this template's.
===============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
---SM-CANCEL-JSON-BEGIN---
{
  "appointment_id": {{ appointment.id | json }},
  "contact_id": {{ appointment.contact_id | json }},
  "contact_name": {{ appointment.contact_name | json }},
  "service": {{ appointment.service.name | json }},
  "scheduled": {{ appointment.scheduled_iso | json }},
  "cancelled_at": {{ appointment.cancelled_at | json }},
  "is_canceled": {{ appointment.is_canceled | json }},
  "owner": {{ appointment.service_agent.name | json }},
  "cancel_reason_id": {{ appointment.cancel_reason.id | json }},
  "cancel_reason": {{ appointment.cancel_reason.name | json }},
  "notes_summary": {{ appointment.notes_summary | json }},
  "customer_notes": {{ appointment.customer_notes | json }},
  "appointment_notes": [
    {%- for n in appointment.notes -%}
    {
      "id": {{ n.id | json }},
      "title": {{ n.title | json }},
      "body": {{ n.body | json }},
      "private": {{ n.private | json }},
      "created_at": {{ n.created_at | json }},
      "created_by": {{ n.created_by.name | json }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ],
  "contact_notes": [
    {%- for n in appointment.contact.notes -%}
    {
      "id": {{ n.id | json }},
      "title": {{ n.title | json }},
      "body": {{ n.body | json }},
      "private": {{ n.private | json }},
      "created_at": {{ n.created_at | json }},
      "created_by": {{ n.created_by.name | json }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
---SM-CANCEL-JSON-END---
